From: Shane de Deuge <shane@scielex.com.au>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mangoh-yellow: power the Cypress WiFi on sdhc_2

Describe WL_REG_ON (SX1509 GPIO 1) as the SDIO slot's supply so the MMC core
powers the CYW43430 before scanning and the kernel owns the line, instead of
a script toggling it from userspace through a Legato-loaded module.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board specific]
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/swi-wp-mangoh-yellow.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/swi-wp-mangoh-yellow.dtsi
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 
 / {
 	model = "Sierra Wireless, Inc. MDM 9xxx WP series - mangOH Yellow";
@@ -78,3 +79,35 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Cypress CYW43430 WiFi/Bluetooth, on the WP's SDIO port (sdhc_2).
+ *
+ * WL_REG_ON is GPIO 1 of the SX1509 expander. It is described as the SDIO slot's supply, so the
+ * MMC core powers the chip before it scans the bus and powers it down when the host releases it;
+ * nothing else touches the line. This is the 4.14 equivalent of the old cywifi.sh sequence
+ * (WL_REG_ON high, wait, then load sdhci-msm), and it keeps the chip's power under the kernel's
+ * control at shutdown. Not covered: DV3 boards, which use WP GPIO33 for WL_REG_ON.
+ */
+/ {
+	wlan_en_vreg: wlan-en-vreg {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "wlan-en";
+		/* matches the qcom,vdd-voltage-level set for sdhc_2 in mdm9607-wp76xx.dtsi */
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <2850000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <2850000>;
+		gpio = <&sx1509 1 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+		/* the old script waited 2 s after WL_REG_ON; the chip needs well under that */
+		startup-delay-us = <250000>;
+	};
+};
+
+&sdhc_2 {
+	vdd-supply = <&wlan_en_vreg>;
+	/* a soldered-down SDIO chip: no card detect, scan once at power-up */
+	qcom,nonremovable;
+	keep-power-in-suspend;
+	pinctrl-0 = <&sdc2_clk_on &sdc2_cmd_on &sdc2_data_on>;
+	status = "ok";
+};
